Q: Failed to compile values file while trying to run in android studio A: <p>In my case, the mistake came from value with ' (single quote) character like this:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;item&gt;Company's Social Media&lt;/item&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>it's should be written with backslash:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;item&gt;Company\'s Social Media&lt;/item&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Hyperlink button in HTML form does not include other form fields in submission payload A: <p>The problem is that you do not actually "submit" the form data. Your button links to the correct controller/method but does not send any data to the controller when you use a link, i.e. <code>&lt;a href=...</code>. You need a submit button.</p>

<p>The change is quite simple. Change the code for the button as follows.</p>

<pre><code>&lt;div class="modal-footer" style="text-align:center;"&gt;
  &lt;input type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" name="addItem" value="Add Item"&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>There is another issue. You have two <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> tags.
Remove the line</p>

<pre><code>&lt;form method ="post" action="&lt;?php echo site_url("Search/addItem"); ?&gt;"&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>And change the line</p>

<pre><code>&lt;form role="form"&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>to</p>

<pre><code>&lt;form method="post" action="&lt;?php echo site_url("Search/addItem"); ?&gt;" role="form"&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>You also need to remove the extra form close tag two lines above the button's code. Nested <code>&lt;form&gt;s</code> are not allowed. And you need to move the closing tag for <code>&lt;div class="modal-content"&gt;</code> So to make it more clear here is what your view should finally look like.</p>

<pre><code>&lt;div id="addItem" class="modal fade"&gt;
  &lt;div class="modal-dialog"&gt;
    &lt;div class="modal-content"&gt;
      &lt;div class="modal-header"&gt;
        &lt;button type="button" class="close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-hidden="true"&gt;×&lt;/button&gt;
        &lt;h4 class="modal-title"&gt;Add an Item&lt;/h4&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class="modal-body"&gt;
        &lt;form method ="post" action= "&lt;?php echo site_url("Search/addItem"); ?&gt;" role="form"&gt;
          &lt;table&gt;
            &lt;tr&gt;
              &lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="text" name="rfid" placeholder="RFID" required/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
              &lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="text" name="itemCode" placeholder="Item Code" required/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
              &lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="text" name="masterCode" placeholder="Master Code" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;/tr&gt;
            &lt;tr&gt;
              &lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="text" name="itemName" placeholder="Item Name" required/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
              &lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="text" name="colorCode" placeholder="Color Code" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
              &lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="text" name="colorName" placeholder="Color Name" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;/tr&gt;
            &lt;tr&gt;
              &lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="text" name="location" placeholder="Location" required/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
              &lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="text" name="makelocation" placeholder="Location Made" required/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
              &lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="text" name="itemCategory" placeholder="Item Category" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;/tr&gt;
            &lt;tr&gt;
              &lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="text" name="materialDescription" placeholder="Material Description" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
              &lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="text" name="supplier" placeholder="Supplier/Vendor" required/&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
              &lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="text" name="checkoutAllowed" placeholder="Checkout Allowed" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;/tr&gt;
          &lt;/table&gt;
          &lt;div class="row personal-info"&gt;
            &lt;div class="col-sm-4"&gt;
              &lt;div class="form-group"&gt;
                &lt;textarea name="itemDescription" placeholder="Insert information regarding the weather this item is suitable for and where it is used"&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;
                &lt;textarea name="Comments" placeholder="Additional Coments on the Item"&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;
              &lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;div class="modal-footer" style="text-align:center;"&gt;
            &lt;input type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" name="addItem" value="Add Item"&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/form&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Go continue jumps over a for iteration A: <p>it's normal that you're not displaying the 5, because i represents the iterator, not the element in the range.<br />
You need to separate the iterator from the element in the range:</p>
<pre><code>func main() {
    for i, v := range []int{1, 2, 3, 4, 5} {
        // i == iterator            (0, 1, 2, 3, 4)
        // v == element in range    (1, 2, 3, 4, 5)
        if v%2 == 0 {
            continue
        }
        fmt.Println(&quot;Itérator: &quot;, i)
        fmt.Println(&quot;Element :&quot;, v)
    }
}

The result :

Iterator:  0
Element : 1
Iterator:  2
Element : 3
Iterator:  4
Element : 5
</code></pre>

Q: When does AsyncLocalStorage get garbage collected? A: <p>In your example, <code>data</code> will become available for GC when the <em>later</em> of the following two things happen:</p>
<ol>
<li><p>The anonymous closure you passed to <code>run</code> finishes.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Any async contexts (e.g. promises, setTimeout callbacks, etc.) created by <code>callBack</code> are no longer referenced (e.g. timers have expired, promises resolved or rejected).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>So if callBack is:</p>
<pre><code>function callBack() {
    setTimeout(() =&gt; {}, 10000);
}
</code></pre>
<p>then <code>data</code> will only be eligible for GC after 10 seconds have passed, since the async context is bound to the <code>setTimeout</code> callback (the runtime can't tell in the general cases whether the callback is going to call <code>context.getStore()</code> or not, so it binds the async context to all created callbacks regardless).</p>
<p>This point is potentially very dangerous - lots of calls to 3rd party APIs (particularly DB driver calls, HTTP api libraries, etc.) create long lived async contexts for things like connection pooling and socket reuse. This can mean async contexts inadvertently persisting for a very long time after the original <code>run</code> call has completed.</p>
<p>You can do a few things to mitigate the issue:</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Only use small objects in <code>AsyncLocalStorage</code> so the leaks don't matter too much</p>
</li>
<li><p>Wrap calls to 3rd party APIs that 'leak' contexts with <code>context.exit</code>. e.g. <code>const stuff = await context.exit(() =&gt; db.fetchStuff());</code> . This is tricky to do, since you have to wrap <strong>every</strong> call - if you miss even one, your context may well leak.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Manually clean up objects stored in <code>AsyncLocalStorage</code>. e.g. if you wanted to store a <code>req</code> object, when the request processing has completed, you can null out the req - you'll have to wrap it in any object, and then <code>delete</code> the key holding the req. e.g.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const reqContext = new AsyncLocalStorage();
function getReq() {
    return reqContext.getStore()?.req || null;
}
function runWithReq(req, callback) {
    return reqContext.run({req}, async () =&gt; {
        try {
            return await callback();
        } finally {
            const store = reqContext.getStore(); 
            delete store['req'];
        }
    });
}
</code></pre>
<p><code>AsyncLocalStorage</code> is powerful, but also potentially dangerous to use for whole requests in complex code bases due to the context leak behaviour.</p>
